WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:06.860
Lost promises to the stars

00:06.900 --> 00:13.100
Memories never fade.

00:22.650 --> 00:26.280
While searching for four-leaf clovers

00:26.320 --> 00:30.520
I steal a glance at your face

00:30.560 --> 00:34.020
And then quickly look away

00:34.400 --> 00:39.360
A gentle rain falls over us

00:39.400 --> 00:42.200
As we meet more people

00:42.240 --> 00:45.230
The more dramatic it gets

00:45.270 --> 00:50.800
Will the day come when we find

00:50.850 --> 00:56.750
Our broken treasures again?

00:56.850 --> 01:02.290
The scars will not fade

01:02.320 --> 01:08.130
We each must go

01:08.160 --> 01:12.220
To where we belong

01:45.570 --> 01:47.600
The map of Japan that
I borrowed from Shin

01:47.600 --> 01:49.370
looked like it had been rained on
multiple times.

01:50.040 --> 01:51.530
It was weather-worn and yellow.

01:51.810 --> 01:53.140
When I opened it up,

01:53.140 --> 01:56.630
the dried-up scotch tape that was
holding it together cracked here and there.

01:57.950 --> 02:02.510
This is like an ancient document.
It's been that long.

02:03.620 --> 02:07.350
Yuta, when you get to Hokkaido,
don't push yourself too hard.

02:08.190 --> 02:11.030
It's a really big place and
there aren't many streetlights

02:11.030 --> 02:13.550
so be sure you secure a place to sleep
before the sun goes down.

02:14.230 --> 02:18.530
And also, you should use the ferry
to cross over to Hokkaido.

02:19.430 --> 02:24.030
You'll be wowed when Hokkaido nears
after some four hours.

02:24.870 --> 02:27.440
You'll get this thrilling feeling
that you're on a "journey"

02:27.440 --> 02:29.970
the moment you ride
your bike onto the ferry.

02:32.050 --> 02:35.680
This red line tracks Shin's journey.

02:37.590 --> 02:41.250
It's like a constellation.

02:54.900 --> 02:56.600
I'm starving...

02:58.740 --> 03:03.770
A school! Where there's a school.
there are shops around!

03:04.410 --> 03:05.310
Bingo!

03:08.820 --> 03:10.280
Hello...

03:11.790 --> 03:15.950
There they are! But only red bean buns?!
Not much of a choice!

03:16.560 --> 03:20.050
But I've finally found an energy source!
I'll secure them all!

03:20.860 --> 03:23.160
Hi there... Welcome!

03:23.570 --> 03:25.230
Hi. I'd like to buy these.

03:25.430 --> 03:28.430
Is that all you're having for lunch?

03:28.470 --> 03:30.230
Huh? Uh, yes...

03:30.640 --> 03:32.130
Where are you from?

03:32.410 --> 03:33.240
From Tokyo.

03:33.370 --> 03:34.710
Tokyo?!

03:42.050 --> 03:43.810
Want some more ham?

03:43.890 --> 03:45.880
Uh, no, thank you...

03:46.450 --> 03:49.150
I'm sorry I only have pickles.

03:49.290 --> 03:52.280
If that's not enough,
I can make some noodles.

03:52.590 --> 03:54.860
This is more than enough.
Thank you so much.

03:56.730 --> 04:02.070
My mother-in-law kept this store.
That's her right there.

04:02.570 --> 04:07.130
And next to her is my father-in-law.
That's my husband.

04:07.740 --> 04:11.640
What are those huge leaves... Aloe?

04:11.880 --> 04:15.980
That's right.
That photo was taken in Los Angeles.

04:16.120 --> 04:18.310
Los Angeles...
You mean in the U. S?!

04:18.650 --> 04:20.420
Huh? You've been there, Granny?

04:20.760 --> 04:23.750
I went there with the people
from farmer's association.

04:24.630 --> 04:27.290
Here's a snack for you.
Take them along.

04:29.500 --> 04:31.430
Wow... She's way ahead of me...

04:31.770 --> 04:34.630
I've never even been on a plane.

04:35.700 --> 04:37.330
But she's been all the way to LA.

04:38.970 --> 04:40.700
An old lady like her...

04:41.180 --> 04:46.510
They were huge...
those aloe leaves were this big!

04:47.380 --> 04:50.780
Even my mom has never
been outside of Japan.

04:52.450 --> 04:53.420
Neither has my father.

04:55.420 --> 04:59.790
That's right. It all ended...
without ever leaving.

05:00.630 --> 05:01.600
Not even once.

05:09.270 --> 05:10.360
That's a...

05:10.710 --> 05:13.230
Dad, this train has a star on it!

05:13.540 --> 05:17.530
Yeah, pretty cool, huh?
The name of this train is...

05:19.880 --> 05:20.970
Northern Star!

05:25.620 --> 05:28.420
Yuta, that's a sleeper car.

05:29.090 --> 05:31.120
It'll take all night to go
all the way to Sapporo.

05:31.690 --> 05:34.390
Let's ride that train together
when you get older.

05:34.730 --> 05:37.030
But Dad, I wanna ride it right now.

05:37.400 --> 05:41.460
No. I mean, you get sleepy
after 10.00 p.m., right?

05:42.170 --> 05:44.430
And that wouldn't be fun for me, right?

05:45.810 --> 05:47.780
Let's ride it together

05:47.780 --> 05:50.510
when you're able to stay up later
and can talk more...

05:51.510 --> 05:53.210
One day...
the two of us together...

06:01.560 --> 06:02.220
Huh?

06:13.370 --> 06:16.830
Th-That was close...

06:36.360 --> 06:37.550
The Milky Way...

06:42.200 --> 06:46.960
A life in which he couldn't even fulfill
his wish of riding that tiny red train...

06:48.370 --> 06:54.100
The meaning of my dad's life... and...
the meaning of my life...

06:58.110 --> 07:01.810
My hands... look fine!
My legs are okay too! No problem!

07:06.290 --> 07:07.120
Let's hit the road.

09:14.820 --> 09:17.610
This is the end of Japan.

09:19.850 --> 09:20.880
It's strange...

09:22.020 --> 09:28.520
You can reach the end of the earth
just by taking a step at a time.

09:30.230 --> 09:36.900
It's so obvious... but I didn't
even realize it... until I got here.

09:38.970 --> 09:41.910
I'm so glad to have been able
to see this landscape...

09:47.850 --> 09:48.820
I'm going home.

09:49.250 --> 09:53.740
To where you and I and our friends live...

09:55.720 --> 10:00.590
I'm going home... pedaling.
Pedaling the same number of times...

10:28.690 --> 10:29.950
Welcome home...

10:39.000 --> 10:40.870
Hagu, I'm gonna go...

10:45.240 --> 10:48.370
August 30th... The end of summer...

10:50.510 --> 10:53.280
No... the last summer break...

10:55.980 --> 10:57.780
Welcome home... Yuta...

11:19.740 --> 11:21.540
Uh. Yuta!

11:21.810 --> 11:23.400
Hey there, you runaway!

11:23.710 --> 11:25.550
Hey, Yuta!

11:25.550 --> 11:28.710
The poster child of adolescence
has returned!

11:31.850 --> 11:35.080
Welcome home. Yuta.
I'm so glad you are safe.

11:35.520 --> 11:37.820
Th-Thank you very much.

11:38.360 --> 11:39.590
Hey, Yuta.

11:41.030 --> 11:44.620
Did you sleep well last night?
You did, didn't you?

11:45.070 --> 11:48.160
With sweet dreams. of course.

11:48.970 --> 11:51.710
I can't pull him away,
so I guess I have to give it a little chop...

11:51.710 --> 11:54.470
- No! Prof. Hanamoto! Calm down!
- Takumi, come here immediately!

11:55.980 --> 11:59.470
You caused a lot of trouble...
You wouldn't wake up.

11:59.980 --> 12:04.620
I'm sorry... I was on a high since
getting back into the Kanto region

12:04.620 --> 12:06.950
and I just barreled along
without getting any sleep.

12:07.820 --> 12:09.150
I'm sorry, Hagu.

12:10.460 --> 12:14.900
And, so how was your trip?
How far did you go?

12:15.360 --> 12:17.020
Um... up to Wakkanai.

12:17.400 --> 12:19.830
Wakkanai? In Hokkaido?

12:20.530 --> 12:22.590
That's the northern end of Japan.

12:22.700 --> 12:26.230
And. how about it?
Did you find yourself?

12:26.370 --> 12:29.310
Did you find the answer?
The truth? Enlightenment?

12:29.480 --> 12:34.120
Well, many people along the way
said the same thing

12:34.120 --> 12:36.750
but I didn't go on this journey
to "find myself."

12:36.750 --> 12:38.050
- What?!
- Huh?!

12:38.190 --> 12:43.280
Really, I was merely frustrated and left,
without thinking.

12:43.420 --> 12:46.720
I just ended up going
farther than I thought...

12:48.430 --> 12:51.970
As I cooked for myself
and got better at sleeping outdoors,

12:51.970 --> 12:57.200
just the act of riding
became interesting to me...

12:58.440 --> 13:01.170
I did some live-in
part-time work along the way.

13:01.710 --> 13:06.340
And met a lot of people.
I thought a lot of different thoughts.

13:07.750 --> 13:12.120
But found nothing
like an "answer" or " myself."

13:13.090 --> 13:15.990
I really came back empty-handed.

13:16.190 --> 13:20.890
Yes, yes! Empty-handed!
Just you and your youth!

13:21.030 --> 13:23.830
You came back with something
called nothing!

13:24.370 --> 13:26.830
Well said! Excellent!

13:26.870 --> 13:29.300
Just stay the way you are!

13:32.010 --> 13:35.030
Yuta, we're having a party tonight.

13:35.140 --> 13:37.200
I'll cook lots of delicious things!

13:38.080 --> 13:39.570
Umm...

13:39.610 --> 13:42.180
How about this?
Instead of having a party,

13:42.180 --> 13:44.020
why don't we all go to
the autumn festival

13:44.020 --> 13:45.420
at Omiya Hachiman Shrine
this weekend.

13:45.950 --> 13:48.080
Let's eat something at the food stalls.

13:48.560 --> 13:51.490
I mean, we haven't gone anywhere
together this summer.

13:51.730 --> 13:55.020
Nice work, Yuta!
Evading the girls' cooking!

13:55.500 --> 13:56.760
Well, I'll be going.

13:57.030 --> 13:59.830
I'm broke, so I better go to
an interview for some part-time work.

14:00.300 --> 14:03.430
You better take a bath
before an interview.

14:04.040 --> 14:07.060
You were out like a light
when you got back last night.

14:07.910 --> 14:09.710
Here's a gift for you
for coming back alive.

14:10.410 --> 14:11.440
Shinobu...

14:13.510 --> 14:14.570
This is...

14:16.550 --> 14:20.790
It's awesome to be able to use
as much water as you want!

14:20.790 --> 14:23.090
- And. it's free! Free!
- Good gracious...

14:23.220 --> 14:24.780
In just his trunks...

14:24.930 --> 14:27.190
Head and body pell-mell...

14:27.660 --> 14:31.460
He's become a wild child...

14:31.930 --> 14:33.900
This feels great!

14:35.540 --> 14:39.600
Huh? Why are you staring
at me like that?

14:39.870 --> 14:41.840
Oh, I was just thinking
you've lost weight...

14:43.880 --> 14:46.640
And this suntan... Not very cool, huh?

14:46.850 --> 14:50.340
Wakkanai, huh? That's so you.

14:50.820 --> 14:54.120
And you didn't even contact us
once in these two months.

14:55.120 --> 14:58.180
I-I'm sorry to make you worried...

14:58.590 --> 15:02.320
Nope! I wasn't worried about you.

15:03.860 --> 15:09.000
You're a pretty tough guy and
I didn't think you'd drop dead that easily.

15:10.140 --> 15:11.040
Shinobu...

15:11.510 --> 15:16.880
Well, getting back to the subject...

15:17.140 --> 15:18.610
Before your interview...

15:19.950 --> 15:21.780
I'll cut your hair for you!
For 1,000 yen!

15:25.020 --> 15:27.580
Are you doubting my love?!

15:27.820 --> 15:30.950
Well, if I believed your love,
wouldn't that be a problem in itself?

15:31.490 --> 15:32.490
Believe it!

15:32.490 --> 15:35.720
- Trust my straight love!
- He's shouting his love to a wet, half-naked man...

15:35.760 --> 15:38.200
- But it's so straight that it passes right through.
- Yeah. How about that?

15:38.270 --> 15:40.290
- And on school property...
- But love is something that penetrates!

15:40.670 --> 15:42.900
Then how about we trim each other?

15:43.040 --> 15:45.230
I can only do close crops, though.

15:45.340 --> 15:47.780
He's fighting back to Shinobu
as an equal...

15:47.780 --> 15:50.040
- He sure has toughened up.
- How about it?

16:00.290 --> 16:01.690
Uh, he's back!

16:02.020 --> 16:05.480
Hey, that was pretty quick!
For going around Hokkaido!

16:06.130 --> 16:09.360
You've got a deep tan.
The tip of your nose is peeling.

16:09.600 --> 16:10.590
Lame!

16:11.730 --> 16:14.860
Got enough money?
Wanna work for two or three days?

16:15.170 --> 16:17.740
Better yet, why don't you make dinner!
And lunch boxes too!

16:17.740 --> 16:19.900
- No problem!
- Great!

16:22.040 --> 16:25.910
Forget about the bike.
Keep it and ride it home.

16:26.610 --> 16:27.880
Also...

16:28.150 --> 16:29.170
Yes?

16:29.480 --> 16:31.150
If you want to work with us,

16:31.150 --> 16:33.780
get a driver's license while
you're still in school.

16:36.360 --> 16:38.260
Oh, Ayu. Where should we start?

16:38.360 --> 16:42.160
Calm down! Let's start with carbs.
Carbs and sauce are calling me!

16:42.230 --> 16:44.990
I'll get Japanese pancakes!
Hagu will get some octopus balls!

16:45.100 --> 16:48.870
Yuta, pan-fried noodles.
Shinobu, corn dogs!

16:48.870 --> 16:50.640
Let's meet here after
we've all bought what we want!

16:50.640 --> 16:52.470
Be sure to load it with sauce!

16:52.610 --> 16:53.600
- Roger!
- Roger!

16:56.580 --> 17:02.640
Hey, Takumi. I think I've seen
the exact same scene last year...

17:03.120 --> 17:04.550
What a coincidence...

17:04.890 --> 17:06.010
I was thinking that too.

17:06.390 --> 17:10.450
I wonder how long I have to
continue being your drinking buddy...

17:14.760 --> 17:16.860
- Missed again!
- I keep missing...

17:17.260 --> 17:19.390
I want a Whip-chan.

17:27.240 --> 17:28.230
Yuta...

17:28.610 --> 17:29.470
What is it?

17:29.810 --> 17:31.070
Go show off yourself.

17:31.410 --> 17:31.970
Huh?

17:32.380 --> 17:34.710
Why don't you do it?

17:35.520 --> 17:39.450
I'm too tired.
I'll go drink with Hanamoto Sensei...

17:40.090 --> 17:41.050
Takumi...

17:43.560 --> 17:46.750
Thanks, Yuta! I'm so happy!

17:46.990 --> 17:48.480
It's so cute!

18:15.220 --> 18:16.950
Hagu, how's your fever?

18:17.720 --> 18:19.090
It's gone down.

18:19.330 --> 18:21.560
I see... that's good.

18:24.300 --> 18:26.730
You traveled far.

18:28.240 --> 18:28.960
Yeah.

18:30.900 --> 18:33.370
What's the end of the earth like?

18:35.480 --> 18:36.700
There was nothing there...

18:37.510 --> 18:40.140
But it was bright.

18:41.250 --> 18:45.710
The sky was beautiful and
I wanted to show it to you, Hagu.

18:47.320 --> 18:50.810
I would love to see it in your painting...
That's what I was thinking.

18:53.630 --> 18:56.960
I'd love to go there too.
I'd love to paint it.

18:59.370 --> 19:02.670
How far could I go
without looking back?

19:04.170 --> 19:05.470
I finally understood...

19:05.470 --> 19:09.410
the reason why I started out
like that that day...

19:10.310 --> 19:13.350
It was probably because
I wanted to learn

19:13.350 --> 19:18.150
just how important everything
I was leaving behind was to me...

19:19.420 --> 19:20.180
Hagu...

19:22.460 --> 19:23.860
I love you...

19:42.940 --> 19:47.440
Yuta... Thank you for coming back...

19:59.930 --> 20:02.990
Your hand was so hot
with the fever

20:03.330 --> 20:06.320
that I started sweating when I held it...

20:07.300 --> 20:10.900
I felt like I was alive.
I felt like I could go on living.

20:11.470 --> 20:13.600
I'm glad I came home.

20:14.010 --> 20:15.570
I really felt that from
the bottom of my heart...

20:17.740 --> 20:21.080
I'll move forward while embracing
everything important to me...

20:22.350 --> 20:27.690
Uncertain futures...
Doubts... Insecurities...

20:28.620 --> 20:30.110
Yearnings that will never
be conveyed...

20:31.120 --> 20:32.680
And desires that will never be fulfilled...

20:34.390 --> 20:36.560
Not being able to
throw down everything...

20:38.030 --> 20:41.130
And the days when
you could find no answers...

20:43.500 --> 20:44.530
I...

20:46.910 --> 20:48.270
What is it. Takumi?

20:48.540 --> 20:51.340
Hurry up, the party's starting.

20:51.550 --> 20:53.380
Okay, I'll be there in a minute.

20:53.850 --> 20:55.780
Yuta, do you have any juice?

20:55.880 --> 20:57.210
Uh, yeah, I have some!

21:03.120 --> 21:07.390
My refrigerator is empty as usual, but...

21:09.000 --> 21:11.230
I don't hear that sound anymore.

21:15.500 --> 21:17.130
I believe...

21:19.440 --> 21:22.640
We'll be able to find what
we all searched for

21:22.640 --> 21:24.340
and couldn't find back then...

21:25.780 --> 21:28.510
One day, for sure...

21:35.860 --> 21:41.950
After rubbing closed eyes

21:42.700 --> 21:48.000
I can see the pastel future

21:48.100 --> 21:54.670
I follow scattered signs

21:55.010 --> 21:58.740
Wearing puzzled expressions

21:58.780 --> 22:04.550
Hey, what were we looking for?

22:04.580 --> 22:07.350
And when was it?

22:07.390 --> 22:15.060
Back when we met, despite our denial

22:15.100 --> 22:21.260
It was like a waltz, so mysterious

22:21.340 --> 22:24.200
At an intersection,

22:24.240 --> 22:27.230
with sunlight shining through the trees

22:27.510 --> 22:30.570
As we turned in time together

22:30.610 --> 22:33.770
The two of us spinning around in a waltz

22:33.810 --> 22:36.870
It was like a waltz

22:36.920 --> 22:39.650
We continue our dance.
